    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the report\r\n\r\nIt looks like `type[item]` is specifically special-cased in CPython so doesn't follow the normal rules:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/188000ae4b486cfffaeaa0a06902e4844d1b2bbc/Objects/abstract.c#L180-L183\r\n\r\n```\r\n        // Special case type[int], but disallow other types so str[int] fails\r\n        if ((PyTypeObject*)o == &PyType_Type) {\r\n            return Py_GenericAlias(o, key);\r\n        }\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I guess Cython will have to add its own specific special-case",
